  "description": "Dusty River uses a simple slate-blue schematic for its room painting. A large title panel spans the upper part of the map, and a turquoise oval represents the water in the centre. Four small dark panels sit in pairs along the left and right edges, surrounded by a faint square grid and a thin ochre border. A pale marked threshold appears at the lower centre. This is an abstract river-location map rather than a detailed view of canyon banks, trees or buildings; the central water symbol and the marked return route are its clearest visual landmarks.",
